[[File:S1E12 Grier Zan Sutos dying.jpg|thumb|Young Grier as his father, [[Zan-Sutos]], dies in his arms]]
Though few were aware, Grier was raised on the secret [[Seeker]] island-nation of [[Sutos Island|Sutos]], where his father, [[Zan-Sutos]], ruled as leader. His family had led the people of this nation to an orderly, happy existence for many years. After his father's death, Grier moved on to the Organization to do his part to bring order to the world using his Seeker skills. With many battles and defeats at the hands of Dante's team, DeFoe lost the favor of the Organization and Grier was chosen to replace him only after he got rid of DeFoe. Grier soon returns to his home and restores order to the island torn apart by war, thereafter being recognized as the new ruler. {{source|Like Father, Unlike Son}}

After the defeat of [[the Professor]], [[Dante Vale]] and his team returned to Sutos Island to ask for help from Grier. His men were attacked by the [[Blood Spiral Brotherhood]]. Grier guided the team through [[The Professor|the Professor's castle]] in order to find the dossier about [[Rassimov]]. Grier later helped Lok Lambert and [[Den Fears]] defeat Mr. Wilder in the Professor's room. As a result of this, he captured Mr. Wilder and took over the Organization. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

